    {
      "id": "SA-S224-letter-i",
      "sequence": 1341,
      "title": "इ — one character, met inside words you already say",
      "headword": "इ",
      "romanization": "i",
      "gloss": "the single character इ — recognised inside words you already say",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-type",
        "writing-block",
        "script-block"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:aeb01a88c214c19d",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [
          "a pen and something to write on",
          "your eyes, for letter shapes on the page"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Script you'll notice: इ",
          "Guided Practice"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You will want a pen and something to write on and your eyes, for letter shapes on the page. You can listen to everything else now — leave the sections called Script you'll notice: इ and Guided Practice until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one, the ones you have already met: ओ, फ, ◌ै. Say what each of them does."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One character this time. One only — and you have been saying it for pages without knowing which mark on the page it was."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: इ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इ — i."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is an independent vowel: the full-size letter a vowel wears when it opens a word and has no consonant to lean on. Inside a word the same vowel is written as a small sign instead."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What it is made of:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a descending upright joined to an upper bowl."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a lower bowl and diagonal tail in the same run."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "the top shirorekhā."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You already say these, and every one of them has इ somewhere inside it:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इदानीम् idānīm — now."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: इ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "1. descend the upright from the headline, turn left around the upper bowl, sweep right through the waist and around the lower bowl, then finish down-right through the tail without lifting."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "2. lift and draw the top shirorekhā left-to-right."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pen lifts: 1. The pen comes up 1 times and no more."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "verified modern printed teaching form; everyday handwriting may simplify the curves."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is one attested teaching order and not a national standard — handwriting here is taught with school-to-school variation. Source: Saurmandal, ‘Devanagari इ stroke order.svg’, panels 1–2, Wikimedia Commons, 5 August 2023."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "at this, and find इ in it",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: at this, and find इ in it]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इदानीम् (idānīm)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "TRACE",
              "instruction": "इ three times, saying i as you finish each one",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU TRACE: इ three times, saying *i* as you finish each one]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "back at any page of this chapter and find इ once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: back at any page of this chapter and find इ once more]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which character is this — इ? What sound does it carry? (i.) Name one word you already say that contains it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
